From a4538111fbeb55d0c4b0368c92686dbe44fdcebf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 18:27:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] skyforge(kne-runtime): startup-config /mnt/flash seed +
 ceos-config identity

Pre-existing Skyforge KNE-runtime delta carried on top of upstream v2.1.2:
startup-config seeding into an emptyDir /mnt/flash (seed init-container
re-materializes the config from its configmap every bringup) and CR-driven
/mnt/flash/ceos-config platform identity (SERIALNUMBER/SYSTEMMACADDR), plus
MAPETH0/MGMT_INTF env defaults and the getPod/getVolumes/getVolumeMounts
signature refactor they require.

task #77: /mnt/flash is an emptyDir, NOT a per-device longhorn PVC. A privileged
cEOS pod sees ALL host /dev/sd* nodes; each attached longhorn volume adds one,
and EOS ssdinit.sh serial-scans (I/O-erroring on foreign devices) every one,
stalling Sysdb past the startup probe budget -> SIGKILL exit137 crashloop. The
change-demo re-seeds startup-config from a configmap each bringup, so durable
per-device persistence is unnecessary; dropping the PVCs removes ~40 host block
devices from the scan. (Removed with it: ensureStartupConfigPVC,
startupConfigPVCName, DEFAULT_STARTUP_PVC_SIZE, the hash/fnv import.)
